{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy gives clear states a forward-progress bias via move_forward, uses random_walk only as a secondary clear-space exploration mode, routes every obstacle observation through dedicated recovery states, uses move_backward only as a brief front-obstacle escape, prefers directed turns away from side obstacles, and returns to forward exploration immediately on path_clear. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not unnecessarily preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in plant automata.",
    "Use one main policy specification with perception states and one-shot action states so each non-perception state enables exactly one controllable action.",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, with occasional random_walk only from a dedicated clear/search branch.",
    "After obstacle_front use a dedicated backward escape once, then a directed turn recovery; after obstacle_left/right use directed turns only.",
    "Make all states total on uncontrollable events and let path_clear quickly return recovery states to forward exploration."
  ],
